---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const repo = "https://github.com/nghxni/lightesb-camel/blob/main";
---

<BaseLayout current="/articles" title="A small-team workflow for external Agents | LightESB-Camel" headline="A small-team workflow for external Agents" description="Start with one existing service and one verifiable change. Let an external Agent draft the candidate while LightESB provides deterministic validation and runtime controls.">
  <article class="article-page">
    <div class="container article-layout">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="solo.eyebrow">Technical article</p>
      <h1 data-i18n="solo.title">A small-team workflow for external Agents</h1>
      <p class="lead" data-i18n="solo.lead">Start with one existing service and one verifiable change. Let an external Agent draft the candidate while LightESB provides deterministic validation and runtime controls.</p>
      <section>
        <h2 data-i18n="solo.s0.title">Choose a bounded first task</h2>
        <p data-i18n="solo.s0.body">Select one HTTP or transformation service and define the expected request, response, and failure behavior. Read the package documentation and the target CLI help before drafting commands.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 data-i18n="solo.s1.title">Keep context outside the runtime</h2>
        <p data-i18n="solo.s1.body">Choose the external Agent and model according to your deployment and data constraints. Store their credentials in that environment. LightESB does not need a model registry or an in-process conversation session to run integration routes.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 data-i18n="solo.s2.title">Work through one candidate at a time</h2>
        <p data-i18n="solo.s2.body">Read and prepare the service through the CLI, edit the candidate outside the watched directory, generate fixed Schemas from the registered message model, and validate the complete file set. A successful static check does not prove business success.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 data-i18n="solo.s3.title">Apply and observe only within scope</h2>
        <p data-i18n="solo.s3.body">After review and authorization, apply the candidate and verify its returned status, service state, and positive and negative business cases. Keep rollback evidence. Production operations and customer migration need their own explicit scope.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 data-i18n="solo.s4.title">Estimate from measured work</h2>
        <p data-i18n="solo.s4.body">Track model usage, review time, environment costs, and maintenance separately. There is no fixed budget or delivery duration implied by this workflow. Reuse verified service patterns to reduce repeated work.</p>
      </section>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${repo}/docs/components/12-ai-chat.md`} data-i18n="solo.guide">Integration and migration guide</a>
        <a class="button" href={`${repo}/docs/cli/01-cli-command-reference.md`} data-i18n="solo.cli">CLI command reference</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <script is:inline>
    window.pageTranslations = {
  "zh": {
    "solo.eyebrow": "技术文章",
    "solo.title": "小团队的外部 Agent 集成流程",
    "solo.lead": "从一个现有服务和一项可验证的改动开始。外部 Agent 编写候选，LightESB 提供确定性校验与运行控制。",
    "solo.guide": "接入与迁移指南",
    "solo.cli": "CLI 命令参考",
    "solo.s0.title": "选择范围明确的首个任务",
    "solo.s0.body": "选择一个 HTTP 或转换服务，明确预期请求、响应和失败行为。编写命令前先读随包文档和目标 CLI 的 help。",
    "solo.s1.title": "把模型上下文留在运行时之外",
    "solo.s1.body": "按部署环境和数据约束选择外部 Agent 与模型，凭据保存在其环境中。LightESB 运行集成路由不需要模型注册表或进程内对话会话。",
    "solo.s2.title": "逐个候选完成闭环",
    "solo.s2.body": "通过 CLI 读取并准备服务，在监听目录之外编辑候选，从已登记报文模型生成固定 Schema，再校验完整文件集。静态检查通过不等于业务成功。",
    "solo.s3.title": "按授权应用并观察",
    "solo.s3.body": "审核并获授权后应用候选，核对返回状态、服务状态以及业务正反例，并保留回滚证据。生产操作与客户迁移需要各自明确的范围。",
    "solo.s4.title": "根据实际工作估算成本",
    "solo.s4.body": "分别记录模型用量、审核时间、环境费用和维护成本。本流程不承诺固定预算或交付时长；复用已验证的服务模式以减少重复工作。"
  }
};
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
